{"base_rate":0.44312169312169314,"brier":0.14082407407407407,"bss":0.4293187648456057,"bss_hi":0.5105190866316855,"bss_lo":0.3365168135856946,"chart":{"base":[636.6,119.1],"fp":[234.6,266.7],"lead":"62,272.9 272,247.4 482,192.6 692,121.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 78% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +15pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 89% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 7%; promised 96% → rained 81%"},"rel":"79.2,436 393.4,273.7 669.8,116.8"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09616402116402117,"ess":354.5865156221453,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Duesseldorf</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Duesseldorf rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>86%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 756 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nDUSSELDORF, 8.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 30 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(14&ndash;60) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>204</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>98</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>87%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>235</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Duesseldorf</b> <span class=\"muted\">DE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>14&ndash;60\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>756 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Duesseldorf &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Duesseldorf\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.06941176470588,380.2156862745098 87.6204081632653,330.0 191.076052631579,204.78947368421052 301.85542857142855,95.87000000000069 366.9983561643836,37.945205479452056 409.6349787234043,18.0 409.6349787234043,24.195744680851078 366.9983561643836,92.79452054794524 301.85542857142855,174.0 191.076052631579,281.42105263157896 87.6204081632653,367.14285714285717 58.06941176470588,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"220.7037037037037\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"220.7037037037037\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.06941176470588,371.29411764705884 87.6204081632653,326.2857142857143 191.076052631579,257.4736842105263 301.85542857142855,179.2 366.9983561643836,147.64383561643834 409.6349787234043,69.11489361702127\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 204 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.06941176470588\" cy=\"371.29411764705884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 98 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"87.6204081632653\" cy=\"326.2857142857143\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 38%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"191.076052631579\" cy=\"257.4736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 69%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"301.85542857142855\" cy=\"179.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 87%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"366.9983561643836\" cy=\"147.64383561643834\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 235 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.6349787234043\" cy=\"69.11489361702127\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(44%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Duesseldorf the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.35).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.355</td><td class='num'>9.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>0.395</td><td class='num'>8.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.454</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.479</td><td class='num'>8.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.22319,"lon":6.77927,"n":756,"n_cities":134,"name":"Duesseldorf","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.000196078431372549,"n":204,"obs":0.029411764705882353,"sig":true},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.08367346938775509,"n":98,"obs":0.15306122448979592,"sig":true},{"hi":0.575,"lo":0.2